        "title": "The Enlightenment and Its Discontents",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Enlightenment (roughly 1688-1800) is the intellectual watershed that produced modernity:\nthe authority of reason over tradition and religion, the belief in progress, the critique of\narbitrary power, and the foundations of liberalism, democracy, and science. Its \"discontents\"\nare the Romantic reaction, the Counter-Enlightenment, and contemporary critiques from\npostcolonial and feminist scholarship."
